<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation. [CORRECTED 20:46 GMT]</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation. [CORRECTED 20:46 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales and all seven repurchase agreements (corrects number of agreements)  whereby it had sought to drain 3.403 billion pesos (corrects amount) from the secondary market on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    346 days   22.99 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    177 days   21.72 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days   20.82 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    400 million     49 days   19.70 pct</p>
<p>    400 million     45 days   19.59 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     31 days   19.05 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     25 days   18.80 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     17 days   18.64 pct</p>
<p>    500 million	7 days   17.96 pct</p>
<p>    153 million	1 day    17.39 pct</p>
<p>(inserting final four lines of table, missing from initial story)</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
